:". 02-28-2023, 06:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T05:42:05-08:00","id":1504036,"title":"","content":"I think they are asking how to bring the various other faction types into working for you.<br /> <br /> Titans: I've been kind of addressing this in my campaign with the Players occasionally running across the opposition ( Aesir Titan Cult). While they have not been able to turn the cultists very often, they have started to understand the motivations for them, and have on occasion, drawn peace between them when something both sides want to make go away or interests converge. The Fatalism of the Aesir actually can make for some more reasonable opponents as they see Raganrok coming and while preparing for it, aren't in a particular hurry as the KNOW it will happen. So they can take a look around and see if something serves their interest or not. And if they can cause and Aesir to do something that advances their interests, so much the better,<br /> <br /> Dragons: This is a bit of a harder one as Dragons really do not have much interest in working with Scions and the Children of the Gods have caused nothing but misery for them. But you might get one or two who might use them for their own purposes. One of my players is playing a Scion of Loki and they have just met a dragon of the Naga Flight. The Dragon, going by the name Mahatma, is interested in that the Scions have met Jormangundr in their travels, noting that the great Lindwyrm has fallen into melancholy but seems to like his 'little brother''s company. The Mahatma is wanting the characters to interact more with Jormangundr to stimulate him out of his funk. For good or ill.<br /> <br /> Denizens: Will really vary from individual to individual. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13091-thewanderingjewels","name":"TheWanderingJewels","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13091_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}